       suerl= .22D+001            !suerl  REAL      km, average Road Length into the footprint. Christen 2011 has a tower height of 26m and long-term-averaged 80% flux isoplets are about 550m away; helsinki has a$
       suehems= .2015D+003                !suehems        REAL    umol_co2 s-1 person-1, human emission of co2 trough respiration, ref:Moriwaki and Kanda, 2004, used also by Christen et al 2010, 2011. Equivalent $
       suehuc= .10D+001           !suehuc REAL      kg_h2o day-1 person-1, human production of water vapour, dayly amount of evaporated water from human metabolism (respiration, transpiration, sweat) and activiti$
       suevc= .115D+000          !suevc  REAL      lt km-1 vehicle-1, urban fuel consumption of a vehicle, ref: Christen 2010 referred to gasoline cars has .115
       suedd= .832D+000          !suedd  REAL      kg lt-1, traffic fuel density, for diesel ref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diesel_fuel has .832
       suewpt= .1242D+001         !suewpt REAL      kg_h2o kg_fuel-1, Water Produced by Traffic fuel combustion. For diesel, from ref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diesel_fuel results that About r=86.1% of the fu$
       suewpb= .1242D+001         !suewpb REAL      kg_h2o kg_fuel-1, Water Produced by Building-heating fuel combustion. For diesel, from ref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diesel_fuel results that About r=86.1% $
       diet= .3500D+004           !diet           REAL      !kcal day-1 person-1, dayly calories in human diet. ref: FAO, WHO, cited in National Geographic Italia, november 2013, says that the average dayly avail$
       sueec= .1563D+003          !sueec  REAL      W person-1, domestic electric consumption pro capita, ref: Istat for Sassari 2011 gives an equivalent 1369.4 kWh year-1 person-1, http://dati.istat.it/Index.asp$
       suehhp= .473D+002           !suehhp REAL      MJ/kg_fuel, Higher Heat Power of combustion of traffic fuel; for diesel 47.3, ref: http://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potere_calorifico; see also Annamalai and Ishwar$
       suelhp= .444D+002          !suelhp REAL      MJ/kg_fuel, Lower Heat Power of combustion of building-heating fuel; for diesel 44.4, ref: http://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potere_calorifico; see also Annamalai an$
       suewth= .025D+000          !suewth REAL      m, thickness of each layer of which wall/roof are composed; the number of layers is equal to nsoil0 in input morphology. Original RDP value for suewth was 0.25m.
       suehbf= .05D+000           !suehbf REAL      m3 m-3, [0,1] heated building fraction, heated volume of a building over total volume. It excludes non-heated volumes like external walls, stairs, lift vain, ga$
       suehep= .30D+002           !suehep REAL      W m-3, HEating Power for unit volume for buildings, for Sassari 30, ref: http://www.stiliac.it/calor/it/area-tecnica/calcolo-fabbisogno-termico.html, http://www$
       suecp= .32523D+001 	!suecp  REAL      !kg_co2 kg_fuel-1, Carbon dioxide Produced by combustion of 1 kg of building-heating fuel. For diesel, from ref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diesel_fuel is found that $
       sueve= .285D+003           !sueve  REAL      !g_co2 km-1 vehicle-1, mean co2 Vehicle Emission, ref: Jarvi et al. (2012) finds typical co2 emission per vehicle class from "VTT: LIISA2010: Road traffic exhau$
!
! generalization to all popdens. / WRF.  Urban biophysics now scales to popdens (as if Sassari enjoys ubiquity).
!      rdp 12 november 2015: area indices should be positive-definite.  / neg signs for suerai and suewai were eliminated and now they are scaled to popdens..
! kind of a mystery as to why these were initially negative; does this suggest that at some point we lived in caves for a spell? ;) 
       suerai= .121D+000*(popdens/.0023D+000)  ! this is now to scale P/P0 based on Sassari (P0). 
       suerai=min(suerai,.9D+000)	! street gap minimum. rai < 1 at all times.
!suerai REAL      !m2 m-2, Roof Area Index, total area occupied by buildings into the footprint, divided by the footprint area. This implicitly suppose flat roofs. For Sassari, w$
       suewai= .20D+001*(popdens/.0023D+000)          !suewai REAL      !m2 m-2, Wall Area Index, total area occupied by external walls (excluding roofs) of buildings (only those in direct contact with external air) into the footpri$
       suewai=min(suewai,.1D+002)		! keep this less than 10.
!
       suebh1= .22D+002           !suebh1 REAL      !--, [0,24] hour after which all Building Heatings are supposed turned off. For Sassari a meaningful value could be 22. If you want building heating turned on e$
       suebh2= .8D+001            !suebh2 REAL      !--, [0,24] hour before which all Building Heatings are supposed turned off. For Sassari a meaningful value could be 8. If you want building heating turned on e$
       suetol= .10D+002           !suetol REAL      !K, temperature tolerance before turning on heating. If external temperature is lower than the chosen tendo (thermostatic temperature inside buildings) but with$
! set wkg vbles to 0.
       suecdfh=.0D+000
       suelhfh=.0D+000
       sueshfh=.0D+000
       suecdft=.0D+000
       suelhft=.0D+000
       sueshft=.0D+000
